# Stops the benchmark server, which is what lets the reader task see the log.
#
# The scripts beside this one record themselves in {bench::done::*}, so this stops the server as soon as the
# curve has reported. Its second trigger is what turns a hung run into a failed one, and it uses no addon
# syntax, so it also runs when the addon is the thing that broke.
#
# The budget is generous because the curve fills and writes a table of up to 10000 rows six times over:
# a run that is merely slow must not be cut off, while one that never reports has to end.

every 5 seconds:
    if {bench::done::curve} is set:
        log "SKRIPTORM_BENCH=DONE"
        stop the server

every 180 seconds:
    log "SKRIPTORM_BENCH=FAIL the benchmark did not finish"
    stop the server
